 Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000901"} "1,000 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000922"} "1,500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000937"} "5,000 metres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000944"} "500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000965"} "1,000 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000986"} "1,500 metres, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "15001001"} "3,000 metres Relay, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "19020588"} "2022"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/2587"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "2,000 metres Mixed Relay, Mixed" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "10 February 2026"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2193"} "Forum di Milano, Assago, Milano, Milano"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/15001008"} "60 from 12 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Placements 1-8 based on A and B final."]] [:tr {:class "records", :style ""} [:th {:style "vertical-align: top;"} "Olympic Record "] [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/19020588"} "2:36.437"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/137698"} "Suzanne Schulting"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148679"} "Xandra Velzeboer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/137699"} "Itzhak de Laat"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148681"} "Jens van 't Wout"] " " [:a {:href "/countries/NED"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NED.png"}] "NED"] " /  5 February 2022 / " [:a {:href "/records/event_name/2587"} "Details"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "For the second edition of this event at the Olympic Games, the title was wide open. Since Beijing, the World title had been won by three different nations: Netherlands (2023), China (2024) and Canada (2025). In addition, the host nation, Italy, was the only one to have won a medal at all three World Championships. This variation was also shown in the 2025/2026 World Tour, where four different countries won a race: China, Canada, Korea and Netherlands, with the latter winning the overall classification."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were no surprises in the quarter-finals, although the United States was lucky to advance despite a fall by " [:a {:href "/athletes/149169"} "Corie Stoddard"] ". The semi-finals were more exciting. In the first heat, the Netherlands’ " [:a {:href "/athletes/148679"} "Xandra Velzeboer"] " crashed out battling for second with China. In the second heat, Stoddard again fell – while leading, also causing the Korean skater to fall. This left the final spots for Canada and the surprising Belgium, which had only made it through the quarter-finals as a time qualifier. Korea filed a protest due to being impeded by the US, but it was disallowed."] "\n\n" [:p {} "After the Netherlands recorded an inconsequential Olympic Record in the B final, the final was again an exciting affair. Defending champion China took the early lead, but when " [:a {:href "/athletes/140241"} "Zhang Chutong"] " went wide in a curve, Italian veteran " [:a {:href "/athletes/109931"} "Arianna Fontana"] " took the lead. China, still in second, then saw " [:a {:href "/athletes/148134"} "Sun Long"] " slip up, now falling back to last place. Italy held on for the home victory, with anchorman " [:a {:href "/athletes/148510"} "Pietro Sighel"] " crossing the line backwards in celebration, ahead of Canada and the surprising Belgians, who had no reserve skaters for the team."] "\n\n" [:p {} "For Italy’s Arianna Fontana it was her 12th Olympic medal in her sixth Olympic Games, four more than any other short track skater. In the Canadian team, " [:a {:href "/athletes/136927"} "Kim Boutin"] " earned her fifth Olympic medal, while " [:a {:href "/athletes/148016"} "Steven Dubois"] " earned his fourth. Belgium’s bronze was the country’s second in the sport, following " [:a {:href "/athletes/147886"} "Hanne Desmet"] "’s bronze in 2022. She was also on this team, along with her brother " [:a {:href "/athletes/111336"} "Stijn De Smet"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Italy"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/140263"} "Elisa Confortola"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/109931"} "Arianna Fontana"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/156708"} "Chiara Betti"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148510"} "Pietro Sighel"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/140289"} "Thomas Nadalini"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148511"} "Luca Spechenhauser"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} "Canada"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/140275"} "Florence Brunelle"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/136927"} "Kim Boutin"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/148015"} "Courtney Sarault"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/156214"} "W